    runtime: an image's methods are activated with membership questions asked in their world
    
    Package loading runs in a fixed older world (`_require_world_age`), and the method table's insertion of an image's
    methods asked its questions about memberships in the task's world: the entries declared in the session, or by the
    images loaded since, were not in force there. A membership's method of a pattern member (`Type{<:Y0}` for a set
    `Y0`) meets the absence edge of a concrete type only through such an entry (`S0 in Y0`), so an image's membership
    of `Y0` in `X` left the code that folded `S0 isa X` to `false` (found by the set-folds report's image mode). Now
    the insertion asks in the world the image's methods begin in, as a declaration's does (compiler §4.11).
    
    Reference: compiler §4.11 (membership queries run at the world being inferred or matched for), §9.
    Test: experiments/implementation/w171/gates/n46_image_activation_world.jl; audit/set_folds_images.jl.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/staticdata.c b/src/staticdata.c
